[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,4.5);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (8.4,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {0.88/4,1.76/8,2.64/12,3.52/16} {\draw (-0.15,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\draw (0.5,0) rectangle (1.5,0.22);
\draw (1.5,0) rectangle (2.5,0.88);
\draw (2.5,0) rectangle (3.5,2.2);
\draw (3.5,0) rectangle (4.5,3.52);
\draw (4.5,0) rectangle (5.5,2.42);
\draw (5.5,0) rectangle (6.5,1.1);
\draw (6.5,0) rectangle (7.5,0.22);
\foreach \x/\lab in {1/5,2/6,3/7,4/8,5/9,6/10,7/11} \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\lab$};
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.3,2.2) {Frequency};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (4,-0.9) {Pieces of fruit per week};
\node[font=\small] at (4,4.8) {Fruit eaten per week};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which statement about this histogram is correct?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-0.3,0) -- (12.2,0) node[below right,font=\scriptsize] {Score};
\draw[thick,domain=0.4:3.6,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*exp(-(\x-2)*(\x-2)/0.4)});
\draw[thick,blue,dashed,domain=3:7.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2*exp(-(\x-5.2)*(\x-5.2)/0.9)});
\draw[thick,red,dotted,domain=5.6:11.6,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1.5*exp(-(\x-8.6)*(\x-8.6)/1.6)});
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (2,3.35) {$X$};
\node[font=\scriptsize,blue] at (5.2,2.35) {$Y$};
\node[font=\scriptsize,red] at (8.6,1.85) {$Z$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Three normal curves are drawn on the same axis with the same scale. Which has the largest standard deviation?

